rhldr_yield":0.08931083080029083,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02047161319291197,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":65.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.21367,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Black Stone Minerals, L.P., together with its subsidiaries, owns and manages oil and natural gas mineral interests. It owns mineral interests in approximately 16.9 million gross acres, nonparticipating royalty interests in 1.8 million gross acres, and overriding royalty interests in 1.6 million gross acres located in 41 states in the United States. The company was founded in 1876 and is based in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. H. Taylor DeWalch | Co-CEO, President & Director of Black Stone Minerals GP L.L.C. | Age 35 | Compensation: $619,375 (FY2025)","financial_summary":["Black Stone Minerals, L.P. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.0B market cap on $470M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 35\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 8.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 21% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 6.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 69% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6884141095497562},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $35.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-35072757.29},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 50% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Analyzing Black Stone Minerals (NYSE:BSM) and CVR Energy (NYSE:CVI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/analyzing-black-stone-minerals-nysebsm-and-cvr-energy-nysecvi.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794539729.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Black Stone Mi